        },
        {
          "say": "Use renewable feedstocks, catalysts, and safer solvents like water.",
          "write": "renewable, catalysts, safe solvents"
        },
        {
          "say": "Run reactions near room temperature to save energy.",
          "write": "energy efficiency"
        },
        {
          "say": "Design products to break down harmlessly after use.",
          "write": "design for degradation"
        },
        {
          "say": "Principles work together. A catalyst can lower temperature and waste.",
          "write": "catalyst → lower T, less waste"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Renewable feedstocks",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A feedstock is the raw material used to make a product.",
          "write": "feedstock"
        },
        {
          "say": "Renewable ones, like sugarcane, regrow within a human lifetime.",
          "write": "sugarcane, corn, oils"
        },
        {
          "say": "Crude oil took millions of years to form. It is non-renewable.",
          "write": "crude oil: non-renewable",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Feedstocks compared",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 230,
                "h": 100,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "sugarcane: regrows"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 300,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 230,
                "h": 100,
                "fill": "grey",
                "label": "crude oil: used up",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "renewable ≠ automatically green",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "But crops need land, water and energy. Renewable is not always green.",
          "write": "consider land, water, energy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Atom economy",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Atom economy asks how much of the reactants ends up in the product.",
          "write": "how much ends up in the meal"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide the product molar mass by all reactants, then times 100.",
          "write": "AE = M(product) ÷ M(reactants) × 100"
        },
        {
          "say": "Use the coefficients from the balanced equation.",
          "write": "multiply by coefficients"
        },
        {
          "say": "Addition reactions put everything into one product. That is 100 percent.",
          "write": "addition → 100%"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Two ways to make ethanol",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Method 1: ethene plus water gives ethanol.",
          "write": "C₂H₄ + H₂O → C₂H₅OH"
        },
        {
          "say": "46 over 46, times 100. That is 100 percent.",
          "write": "AE = 100%",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Hydration atom economy",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 500,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "ethanol 46.0 (all of it)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "100%",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "green",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Method 2: fermenting glucose makes ethanol and carbon dioxide.",
          "write": "C₆H₁₂O₆ → 2C₂H₅OH + 2CO₂"
        },
        {
          "say": "92 over 180 gives 51.1 percent. The rest is wasted as C O 2.",
          "write": "AE = 92.0 ÷ 180.0 = 51.1%",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Fermentation atom economy",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 255,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "2 ethanol 92.0"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 285,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 245,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "grey",
                "label": "2 CO₂ 88.0",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "51.1%",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "orange",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "But method 2 uses a renewable feedstock at mild temperatures.",
          "write": "renewable, mild conditions"
        },
        {
          "say": "So judge greenness by several principles, not one number.",
          "write": "weigh several principles"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Atom economy is not percentage yield. Yield compares actual to possible.",
          "write": "AE ≠ % yield"
        },
        {
          "say": "A 100 percent yield can still have a low atom economy.",
          "write": "100% yield, low AE possible"
        },
        {
          "say": "Forgetting coefficients gives the wrong atom economy.",
          "write": "use coefficients"
        },
        {
          "say": "Name the principle. Do not just say better for the environment.",
          "write": "name the principle"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Prevent waste, do not clean it up.",
          "write": "prevention first"
        },
        {
          "say": "Linear is a line to the bin. Circular is a loop.",
          "write": "linear vs circular"
        },
        {
          "say": "PRODUCTIVELY for the 12 principles.",
          "write": "PRODUCTIVELY"
        },
        {
          "say": "Atom economy: product over all reactants, times 100.",
          "write": "AE = product ÷ reactants × 100"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
